extraction_notes: |
  - Rifts World Book 4: Africa, printed 61-63 (cache p062-p064). The race
    intro starts at the foot of printed 61, the stat block is printed 62 and
    runs onto printed 63, which also holds magic, skills, life span, habitat
    and the Anhur note; the Tautons begin lower on printed 63. Printed 64 is
    all Tauton, so the source ends at 63 (the brief said 61-64). Printed 62
    and 63 were checked against 110 dpi renders and agree with the text
    layer on every number. The Minions of the Gods intro on printed 59-60
    adds only that these optional R.C.C.s may be player characters and that
    good members of evil races are renegades; nothing mechanical.
  - XP: the "Pygmy Shaman & Ramen" ladder on printed 160, read off a 150 dpi
    render: upper bounds 2,050 / 4,100 / 8,250 / 16,500 / 24,600 / 34,700 /
    49,800 / 69,900 / 95,000 / 130,100 / 180,200 / 230,300 / 280,400 /
    340,500 / 400,600, stored as the fifteen lower bounds.
  - POOLS: M.D.C. 1D4x100 is `mdc_base`, the race being a mega-damage
    creature; with it stated there is no `men_of_arms` line. No hit points or
    S.D.C. are printed. P.P.E. 1D6x10+40, +6 per level; I.S.P. 1D6x10+40,
    +1D6+1 per level.
  - PSIONICS: printed 62 heads the list "Standard Psi-Powers", a fixed set
    rather than a tier, and the catalog''s tiers are only minor, major and
    master. Stored as master because the set includes Empathic Transmission,
    a Super power only a master gets (a judgement call). The
    seven powers are granted by name and none are picked: Empathic
    Transmission (Super), Empathy, Presence Sense, Nightvision, Bio-
    Regeneration (the Healing row, not the Super one), Mind Block, and the
    racial Psionic Empathy with Animals (category Special).
  - MAGIC, THE 40%: "40% are effectively mystics, except select only 4
    spells at first level and 2 spells at second level and every level
    thereafter", P.P.E. as the race. Stored as a choose-1 between two
    abilities, not as variants, because a variant cannot carry `magic`
    (VARIANT_OVERRIDES); the Amazon''s Magic Powers ability is the model. The
    percentile is recorded in the ability names (01-40 / 41-00) and in a
    restriction line telling the player to roll; nothing in the app rolls
    it. The level caps are the Mystic''s (levels 1-2 at first level, 1-3 at
    second, 1-4 at third, then up to the character''s level), as the live
    mystic and the Amazon store them; only the counts are the Ramen''s. The
    Mystic''s magic bonuses (+2 vs horror factor, +1 vs magic at 3/6/9/12,
    +1 spell strength at 4/8/12) are applied to the mystic branch, reading
    "effectively mystics" as the Mystic''s magic powers with the spell counts
    and P.P.E. replaced (the Amazon precedent); the Mystic''s O.C.C.
    abilities and psionics are not granted. Spell strength is prose.
  - BONUSES: +3 initiative; "+1 on all saving throws" as +1 on each of the
    fifteen d20 saves the sheet draws (the gargoyle precedent), not coma/
    death, which is a percentage. Impervious to mind control and half damage
    from psionic attacks are natural abilities, not save bonuses. The +20%
    to ride or work with domesticated animals is conditional and is prose.
  - SKILLS: the R.C.C. prints its own skill list and secondary skills and no
    O.C.C. is mentioned, so the list is stored as printed and the race is
    played as itself (the Grimbor and Shaydor shape). No occ_restrictions,
    since the book neither allows nor forbids an O.C.C. Basic math is
    Mathematics: Basic 45+20; "reads and speaks Dragonese (+20%)" is
    Language: Dragonese 50+20 and Literacy: Dragonese/Elven 30+20; Gobblely
    50+20; Ancient Egyptian (+20%) is a fixed Language: Other at 70 with no
    per-level gain (no catalog row; regression F34 rule). Climb is Climbing
    40+10, prowl 25+10, intelligence 32+20, wilderness survival 30+10,
    horsemanship is Horsemanship: General 40+15. "Track (+10%)" names no
    quarry and is stored as Tracking (people) 25+10, a judgement call (the
    Tauton beside it separates humanoids and animals). Boxing is NOT granted:
    the Combat line ("martial arts and boxing") describes the NPC average,
    and the R.C.C. skill list (printed 63) names only martial arts - the same
    reading the Tauton takes of its identical line. No Hand to Hand upgrade price is
    printed, so no hand_to_hand block.
  - Ancient and modern W.P.s are choices from lists of catalog rows, split by
    judgement: archaic hand weapons, bows and shields on one side, firearms
    and energy weapons on the other. Two technical or communications skills
    are a choose 2 across both categories.
  - SECONDARY: five from any category except Electrical, Medical and
    Science, plus one additional Earth language, stored as a Language: Other
    pick at the catalog base with no bonus. Related skills: none printed,
    none stored.
  - No equipment and no money are printed; neither is stored.
