# Ramen

## Lore

Ten thousand years ago, on a dying world in another dimension, a feline race
and a reptilian race were fighting each other to extinction when the beings
now called the Egyptian gods offered each side salvation and power in return
for service. Both accepted. The felines who swore to the pantheon of Ra became
the ramen, the Knights of Ra; the reptiles who swore to the pantheon of Taut
became the tautons. Their war left their homeworld and has been fought across
the Megaverse ever since.

Ramen are giant humanoid lions, male or female, always tan, often mistaken for
kinnie-ger or werepanthers though far nobler in bearing. They seldom start a
fight unless attacked or ordered to by one of Ra''s pantheon. Most are brave and
compassionate, regarded as valiant knights in the service of Ra and the Gods of
Light. They share an uncanny rapport with animals, and some two in five of them
carry an intuitive, mystic gift for magic.

Ramen prefer forests and wilderness. A few tribes, each of 3D4x10 members,
live in Africa, Turkey, Afghanistan and India. Their allies are the Egyptian
Gods of Light and other champions of good; their enemies are supernatural
monsters, demons and all evil, above all the tautons, whom they attack in
preference to any other foe.

## GM Notes

Many ramen believe the lion-headed Anhur, once a god of light and Ra''s ally, is
their progenitor, and hope he will one day return to the side of good; they
oppose him only with great reluctance. Anhur denies any kinship, yet has more
than once gone to great lengths to protect ramen champions out of respect for
their courage. About 10,000 ramen serve in Anhur''s army (mostly levels 1D4+6,
aberrant or unprincipled). Some two million actively serve the Pantheon of Ra,
often seen with Ra, Isis and Horus, and another twenty million are scattered
across the Megaverse. A renegade band of 57 lives in Egypt, loyal to Pharaoh
Rama-Set''s death cult.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ramen');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'ramen';

